{"id":"deae024a6879a6b99f1816297a79615e452ba76da8f3d886e50b5c8ee5fcc63b","pubkey":"1ea4ae8405ad5c6bd0dc35a0ac83e548c485142538e1e0c54ad40e5bb59a2ae8","created_at":1782025567,"content":"📇⬇️ policy:\n\ncanada\n\n-pesticide ban erosion is a mercosur attachment. you need to consider the reality of trying to cozy up to the eu is being subject to eu regulations and terrible policy being shoved down allies theoats, like mercosur. \n\n-poor forrest management is a serious problem. correcting decades of mismanagement across north america is rooted in nafta funding rhetoric which pulled focus away from conservation and healthy wild spaces in favor of \"industry\". \n\n-https://www.parl.ca/documentviewer/en/45-1/bill/C-29/first-reading?col=2\nan financial crimes agency for white collar crime and crypto disregulation is worthwhile. the language surrounding tokenization is vague and i see the reading which demands government protection of stablecoins as something which canada is forested to enforce. tokens and coins in context of financial crimes is human dna and id trade - difficult to know how the government intents to \"regulate\" that. rhetoric gets you into trouble like in cowichan...\n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/live/UDHNqRKDPKg?si=EY-rYNXMWY9oN4IA\n\n\n-everyone can carry until fall, i will be around watching home time etc. 🫡✌🏻\nhttps://www.youtube.com/live/uE2MOM5-Atc?si=F59ao0zPS2zZuggF\n\n-the culture pass is fab and i supported it in paris and signed it for rachida dati too. signed. \n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/live/Tc3Zr46GuII?si=ijimtE6zEktCa6eM\n\n-organized crime is an immigration issue not a domestic legal one; you need to be aligning intelligence community intel, immigration, and travel agencies.... lawfare and changing domestic laws is a secondary solution to a problem which will not vanish because of it. immigration enforcement is also only a piece. importing labor markets is a british standard practice and one which canada unfortunately adopted in the 90s and again during covid; not because immigration is negative but because literally farming out labor is a mentality which scaffolds labor significance and one which has resulted in the canadian system being unable to feed itself.... or have a sustainable longevity for medical professionals etc. really important to deescalate the rhetoric\nsurrounding \"the other\" and recalibrate the respect for work at all levels of society.  \nhttps://globalnews.ca/news/11818864/bc-government-cracking-down-gun-violence-organized-crime/\n\n-reminder 📇⬇️ policy:\n\nhabeus corpus already covers the conversation attempting to be interwoven into \"private property laws\". the rhetorical effort to erode the boundary between human and property is a quiet creep pumped by fintech - in order to validate token markets and human sale over the counter: slave trade. habeus corpus answers the human sovereignty conversation in the property rights shadow docket. you don't need to litigate it again - which begs the question what the agenda really is regarding this case; or is it genuine incompetence. \n\nhttps://www.justice.gc.ca/eng/csj-sjc/rfc-dlc/ccrf-ccdl/check/art10c.html\n\ncanada needs to return to the awareness of plain meaning and common law in order to avoid entrapping themselves in the mess they are in regarding bc - \nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plain_meaning_rule?wprov=sfti1\n\nhttps://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_law?wprov=sfti1#Comparison_with_statutory_law\n\nnostr:nevent1qqsg45qm8ts9pg6jg08722khxwm2w9ugt503g2aetqczechm9ysuaegpzemhxue69uhhyetvv9ujuurjd9kkzmpwdejhgqgjwaehxw309ahx7um5wgh85cny9enkwqg4waehxw309aex2mrp0yhxummnw3ezumt0v5q35amnwvaz7tmjv4kxz7fwdehhxarjd93ksetn9ehhyecxva3lk\n\nnostr:nevent1qqs0wpy478u4pe4m7zy6m9ydpgkafhyj23g29p933gj7ku0xwntuy2qpzfmhxue69uhkummnw3ezua3sdshxjmcppamhxue69uhkumewwd68ytnrwgq3wamnwvaz7tmxd9k8getj9ehx7um5wgh8w6twv5q3wamnwvaz7tmwdaehgu3wvekhgtnhd9azucnf0gyptah2\n\ncarney: you're ridiculous and you know you're being hyperbolic about protecting private property \"at all costs\". canadian expropriation is one of the most liberal in the g20. and it could be argued the double standard of telling lawyers not to defend property rights and also standing in the house and saying you support private property is of particular benefit to the fintech markets you represent - which includes the misappropriated allocation of land under the confused reading to indigenous groups.... and then use expropriation to seize it for development, and receive even less push back because they are underrepresented communities. i doubt seriously your private donors care about anything other than eventual seizure - \nhttps://laws.justice.gc.ca/eng/acts/E-21/page-1.html#h-211935\n\nhttps://publications.gc.ca/collections/collection_2023/spac-pspc/P4-116-2023-eng.pdf\n\n-signed. https://www.justice.gc.ca/eng/csj-sjc/pl/c16/index.html\n\n-the opioid crisis is simplified into not being a crisis by cleaning up medical prescription distribution and changing controls on prescription drugs. drug distribution is out of control in canada and enabling user sites absolutely became a terrible policy. the reality of the eth networks being toxic to smart tech users needs to be demystified and discussed as if it was a serious problem instead of a taboo. it belongs in financial crimes and sexual violence law as well as environmental law and common law - not to mention it is a war crime to use poison gas on your own citizens.... if we want to rhetorics. consider that carefully. \n\nhttps://www.youtube.com/live/Tc3Zr46GuII?si=jgBwpT0_9I8zo-qv\n\n-clean water bill signed. \n\n📰☕️","tags":[["e","372e574dc12f6670b36e6a5b2e431c94d6e2c15e25493a9a50bfb16423c1cbb7","","root"],["e","5e10b182b6b4ac9a3ce2e7be64045e7b01f57abe508ce23067a416ce052f72e9","","reply"],["r","https://www.parl.ca/documentviewer/en/45-1/bill/C-29/first-reading?col=2"],["r","https://www.youtube.com/live/UDHNqRKDPKg?si=EY-rYNXMWY9oN4IA"],["r","https://www.youtube.com/live/uE2MOM5-Atc?si=F59ao0zPS2zZuggF"],["r","https://www.youtube.com/live/Tc3Zr46GuII?si=ijimtE6zEktCa6eM"],["r","https://globalnews.ca/news/11818864/bc-government-cracking-down-gun-violence-organized-crime/"],["r","https://www.justice.gc.ca/eng/csj-sjc/rfc-dlc/ccrf-ccdl/check/art10c.html"],["r","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Plain_meaning_rule?wprov=sfti1"],["r","https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Common_law?wprov=sfti1#Comparison_with_statutory_law"],["r","https://laws.justice.gc.ca/eng/acts/E-21/page-1.html#h-211935"],["r","https://publications.gc.ca/collections/collection_2023/spac-pspc/P4-116-2023-eng.pdf"],["r","https://www.justice.gc.ca/eng/csj-sjc/pl/c16/index.html"],["r","https://www.youtube.com/live/Tc3Zr46GuII?si=jgBwpT0_9I8zo-qv"]]}
